WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.220
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.040
The Pokémon World Championships...

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.280
A trial to crown
the greatest Pokémon battler.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.390
In the hopes of battling Dande,
the current Supreme Monarch,

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.220
Satoshi is participating
in the Championships.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.900
Trainers from all over the world
are taking part.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.650
They battle other trainers
in their class,

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.580
and the results of those battles...

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:46.240
...determine their
current ranking in the world.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:52.310
Satoshi is currently ranked 415th,
which places him in the Super Class.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:55.490
His path to the Monarch Dande
remains a long one.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.040
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:04.080
Today, he is once again
training for battle.

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.900
You’re really pumped, Kamonegi!

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:37.120
That was some crazy power...
I really felt that...

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.690
Satoshi!

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:46.890
What’s up, Go?

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:50.420
Check it out!
There’s an Ishitsubute outbreak!

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.430
If I can catch Ishitsubute,

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:57.680
then I can evolve it and register both
Gorone and Gorogna in one fell swoop!

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.110
Where’s it happening?

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:00.080
Here.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:01.780
Rock Tunnel, huh?

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.680
Kamonegi, this’ll be a perfect chance
for you to train.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:05.640
Let’s go!

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.140
Rock Tunnel, Kanto Region

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:49.100
Here we are at Rock Tunnel!
Rock Tunnel, Kanto Region

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.500
Where’s that Ishitsubute outbreak?
Rock Tunnel, Kanto Region

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.460
Where’s that Ishitsubute outbreak?

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.760
Huh? I don’t see them.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.670
Did they already leave?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.640
Watch out!

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.600
Go, are you okay?

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.920
Yeah. Thanks, Aceburn.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.120
Be careful, Kamonegi.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.840
Looks like its training
is going well.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.870
Yeah. How’s your search going?

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:46.270
I don’t see any Ishitsubute...

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:54.770
There!

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.610
Monster Ball, go!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:11.360
Ishitsubute’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:16.440
I got Ishitsubute!

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:23.030
Ishitsubute! Rock Pokémon!
Rock/Ground type!

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:25.300
Commonly found near
mountain trails and the like!

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.980
If you step on one by accident,
it gets angry! Beware!

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.340
Another new friend!

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:35.200
Thank you, Kamonegi!
I owe you one.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.520
All’s well that ends well,
I guess.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:49.220
Talk about power!

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.970
Yeah. My Kamonegi is aiming
to be a Leek Master!

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:54.400
Leek Master?

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.540
Yup.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:58.340
The mightiest Kamonegi,
expert at fighting with the leek!

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:02.370
Let’s chase after
that goal together!

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:14.730
Good... You’ve got
some intense power...

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.030
Leek Master... Really?

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.870
This is an official
battle announcement.

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:28.660
Hard at work, I see!

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:34.670
Is that guy participating
in the Pokémon World Championships, too?

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:41.800
Very good! It’s well trained!

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.180
It’s irresistible!

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:45.420
Um...

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.110
Kamonegi!

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.070
Perfect timing, Dotekkotsu!

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:05.170
I was watching your Kamonegi, kid!

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:06.820
It wields its leek well!

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.410
Your Dotekkotsu handles
that steel beam well, too!

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:13.750
Right? So then there’s
only one thing to do!

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.980
You’re in the Super Class,
right, kid?

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:17.710
Yeah. You, too?

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.710
I am Genba!

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:25.950
Dotekkotsu and I have trained hard together!
You can call me Genba the Self-Made Man!

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:33.640
The Pokémon World Championships
has approved this Super Class battle!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:37.980
The match-up is Contestant Satoshi
VS Contestant Genba.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:43.000
This battle will be a 1v1.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.630
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:47.560
3!

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:48.400
2!

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.350
1!

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:49.820
Go!

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.700
Go, Dotekkotsu!
Go, Kamonegi!

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:03.950
Dotekkotsu! Muscular Pokémon!
Fighting type!

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.630
It skillfully wields its steel beam!

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:10.190
It excels at demolition;
construction is not its forte!

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.560
Battle, start!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.240
Here we go...
Crossroad Kill!

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:31.910
100,000 Horsepower!

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.300
Kamonegi!

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:52.680
How’d you like that?
Our 100,000 Horsepower!

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:55.930
Tremble at our skill
with the steel beam!

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:03.810
Good, Kamonegi!
Use Crossroad Kill again!

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.130
Counter with Focus Blast!

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:18.250
Argh...

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.310
Consecutive Cut!

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:25.170
On your feet, Dotekkotsu!
Focus Blast again, and make it count!

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:49.280
Keep pushing them back,
Kamonegi!

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:58.720
It’s predicting Kamonegi’s moves...
Dotekkotsu is more skilled!

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.340
Use Crossroad Kill!

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:08.500
Now!

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:10.630
Get back up!

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:13.380
Brutal Swing!

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:31.000
Kamonegi!

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:33.810
Verifying condition.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:40.200
Scanning... Scanning...
Scanning...

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:52.220
Kamonegi!

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.340
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.200
Battle, resume!

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.250
Kamonegi!
Focus Energy!

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:32.920
It’s fully charged!

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:34.000
You good to go?

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.490
Very good... Looks like
things are gonna keep heating up!

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:59.240
Wait, Kamonegi!
You can’t just charge in carelessly!

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:07.960
Well, then... Crossroad Kill!

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.460
Bring it!
Focus Blast!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:18.630
Fire!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.270
Yeah! That landed!

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:34.020
Okay!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.860
Gah... That really stung!

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.010
Kamonegi! Let’s win this battle
and get a streak going!

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:59.060
I can’t lose here!

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:02.640
We’ve been itching to battle
strong trainers!

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.520
So let’s give it our all!

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:06.310
Build Up!

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:12.100
Focus Energy!

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:25.160
Brutal Swing!

00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:46.180
We’re not even close to done!
Keep swinging!

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:52.310
You seriously believe a steel beam
can lose to a leek?! Send ‘em flying!

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.580
Push back, Kamonegi!

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:25.010
We’re comparing strength?
Sounds wonderful! I accept your challenge!

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:51.950
What?!

00:14:58.720 --> 00:14:59.720
What?!

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:16.650
Dotekkotsu is unable to battle!
Kamonegi wins!

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:20.650
As such, the winner is
Contestant Satoshi!

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.530
All right!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.320
Kamonegi, you did it!

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.340
That steel beam slice was amazing!

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:32.170
We went and lost...

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:36.920
Based on the results of this battle,

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:41.370
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:46.220
It went up!

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.650
You’re 381st!

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:51.720
Your name was Satoshi, right?

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:54.600
I suppose we still have
a long way to go.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:57.600
We’ll have to start training again,
Dotekkotsu.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:01.410
Here.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:08.830
Don’t be so down, Dotekkotsu.
I’ll make you a new steel beam.

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:11.470
Until then, you can use this!

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.450
Good for you, Dotekkotsu!

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.270
Hey!

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:32.850
It’s got a look that screams
that it’s hungry for more battle!

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:39.360
Where are you going?

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:43.730
Kamonegi!

00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:53.320
Kid, it’s got the eyes
of a real warrior!

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.710
I can tell.

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:55.960
Warrior?

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.370
Kamonegi?

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:01.350
Its resilience is quite alluring.

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:04.160
It’s a Pokémon well worth raising!

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.590
You think so, too?

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:09.260
You see?

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.470
Wait, Satoshi!

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:19.330
See ya, kid!

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.260
It <i>just</i> finished a battle.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:40.940
Isn’t it tired?

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:42.950
But it’s gotten closer
to being a Leek Master.

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:45.680
It sliced a steel beam!

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.470
Earlade?!

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:54.730
A wild one?!

00:17:56.800 --> 00:18:01.180
Earlade! Blade Pokémon!
Psychic/Fighting type!

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.180
When trying to protect someone,

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:07.650
it extends its elbows
as if they were swords and fights savagely!

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:11.500
All right! I’ll catch it!

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:14.720
I’m afraid he’s my partner.

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.240
You’re rather inadequate.

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:24.520
I was observing your battle.

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:26.790
The one just now?

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:29.000
Your Kamonegi...

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:32.380
It was rough and unrefined,
and didn’t seem at all aware of its surroundings.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:36.210
But due to sheer power,
it won in spite of its inadequacy.

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:38.890
Are you here to offer advice?

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:40.360
Perhaps...

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:43.620
Even I don’t know why I felt compelled
to come lecture you.

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:46.340
I just couldn’t let you be.

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:49.590
Hi there, Kamonegi.
My name is Rinto.

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:51.860
I am this Earlade’s trainer.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.950
How would you like to battle us?

00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:00.430
You up for it, Kamonegi?

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:05.670
Kamonegi doesn’t seem to understand
that which is most essential.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:08.170
Most essential?

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:10.520
Part of battling
is learning what that is.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.300
Here we go, Earlade.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:18.180
Kamonegi, show them how strong you are!
Crossroad Kill!

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:38.410
Keep it up, Kamonegi!

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:53.560
Use Brutal Swing!

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:55.470
Blunt Edge Strike!

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.480
Kamonegi!

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:22.830
It’s over.

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.660
Kamonegi!

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:28.250
Hang in there, Kamonegi!

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:37.890
Your Kamonegi...

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:40.590
I believe it holds immense potential.

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:42.540
A shame about its inadequacy.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.850
Should we ever meet again,

00:20:44.850 --> 00:20:47.480
I hope to see you
battling in unison.

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:49.990
Shall we go, Earlade?

00:20:57.420 --> 00:20:59.370
Okay, let’s do this!

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:01.820
Huh? Leeks?

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:04.820
Kamonegi!

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:06.680
We won’t let up!

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:09.420
We’ll definitely beat that guy
the next time we meet!

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:10.940
Let’s train together!

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:12.500
But why leeks?

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:16.800
Rinto said he wanted us
to battle in unison.

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:20.720
So if we train using leeks,
maybe I’ll understand Kamonegi better!

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:22.500
Is that how it works?

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:27.010
Aim to be a Leek Master!

00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:35.190
What will the meeting with
the mysterious trainer Rinto and Earlade...

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:38.190
...bring about in
Satoshi and Kamonegi?

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:42.140
Become stronger before your
next encounter, Kamonegi!

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:51.730
Mew!

00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:52.480
Warrgle!

00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:53.270
Runpappa!

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:54.040
Pawou!

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:54.780
Ulgamoth!

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:55.570
Strike!

00:21:55.570 --> 00:21:56.370
Cresselia!

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:57.080
Amakaji!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:57.890
Jirachi!

00:21:57.890 --> 00:21:58.690
Chobomaki!

00:21:58.690 --> 00:21:59.460
Kibago!

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:00.230
Gonbe!

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:01.010
Bayleaf!

00:22:01.010 --> 00:22:02.510
Freezer!

00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:03.700
Zacian!

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:20.550
Mew!

00:22:20.550 --> 00:22:21.380
Wooper!

00:22:21.380 --> 00:22:22.100
Pachirisu!

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:22.950
Sunaba!

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:23.610
Absol!

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:24.470
Lunala!

00:22:24.470 --> 00:22:25.280
Rabbifoot!

00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:26.060
Tropius!

00:22:26.060 --> 00:22:26.830
Sunahebi!

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:27.700
Vibrava!

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:28.350
Burshamo!

00:22:28.350 --> 00:22:29.120
Mokuroh!

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:29.940
Rotom!

00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:30.660
Mooland!

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:31.440
Dodorio!

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:32.160
Otosupus!

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:32.980
Swanna!

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:33.730
Nazonokusa!

00:22:33.730 --> 00:22:34.550
Samehada!

00:22:34.550 --> 00:22:35.320
Darkrai!

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:36.000
Iwanko!

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:36.830
Cortoise!

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:37.660
Scorupi!

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:38.440
Pippi!

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:39.160
Pinpuku!

00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:39.940
Kunugidama!

00:22:39.940 --> 00:22:40.680
Mankey!

00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:41.490
Kimori!

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:42.310
Ligray!

00:22:42.310 --> 00:22:43.740
Rayquaza!

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:44.470
Zamazenta!

00:23:07.140 --> 00:23:09.580
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.580 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:13.040
You’re kidding!

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:15.270
There’s Digda all over the field!

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:17.880
There’s Dugtrio, too!

00:23:17.880 --> 00:23:21.130
Seems they’re causing trouble
by eating the vegetables.

00:23:21.620 --> 00:23:23.670
Wait... Where’d they go?

00:23:23.670 --> 00:23:27.230
We can’t catch them
if they tunnel underground!

00:23:29.430 --> 00:23:31.380
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:32.720
Hands-On Agriculture Studies!

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:34.290
Where is Digda?!
